rved cysteines with a defined disulfide-bonding pattern (Zhang et al., 2010 [PubMed 19653121]).[supplied by OMIM, Apr 2010].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q86Y78","text":"Acts as a modulator of nicotinic acetylcholine receptors (nAChRs) function in the brain (PubMed:27344019, PubMed:34631692). Inhibits nicotine-induced Ca(2+) influx through nAChRs (PubMed:27344019). In vitro, specifically inhibits alpha-3:beta-4 and alpha-7 nAChR currents in an allosteric manner (PubMed:34631692). Acts as a positive regulator of Wnt/beta-catenin signaling (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}